## Answer

To register particle attributes with `ParticleBase` so they are communicated on MPI domain redistribution (migration), you use the **`addAttribute()`** method of `ParticleBase`. 

### Required Usage Pattern

```cpp
// 1. Declare your attribute as a member or local variable
particle_position_type myAttr;  

// 2. Inherit from ParticleBase in your class definition
template <typename T, unsigned Dim = 3>
class MyParticleContainer : public ippl::ParticleBase<...> { ... };

// 3. Call addAttribute() before calling update() or migration:
this->addAttribute(myAttr);
```

### Key Implementation Details (from `src/Particle/ParticleBase.h`)

The declaration at line 186-191 shows the signature that receives attributes during registration:

```cpp
template <typename MemorySpace>
void addAttribute(detail::ParticleAttribBase<MemorySpace>& pa);
```

### Example from Codebase (from `alpine/ParticleContainer.hpp`)

In practice, you typically declare multiple attributes and register them all in a dedicated method like this:

```cpp
ippl::ParticleAttrib<double> q;   // charge attribute  
typename Base::particle_position_type P;  // position velocity
typename Base::particle_position_type E;  // electric field at particle position

void registerAttributes() {
    P.set_name("velocity");
    q.set_name("charge"); 
    E.set_name("electric_field");

    this->addAttribute(q);   // registers for migration
    this->addAttribute(P);   // registers for migration  
    this->addAttribute(E);   // registers for migration
}

ParticleContainer(Mesh_t<Dim>& mesh, FieldLayout_t<Dim>& FL) 
    : pl_m(FL, mesh, fem) {
        this->initialize(pl_m);
        registerAttributes();  // <-- Must be called before first update()
        setupBCs();
    }
```

### Important Notes (from manual section in `data/raw/ippl/manual/ippl_particles.tex`)

- **Timing matters**: Call `addAttribute()` after declaring attributes and calling `initialize()`, but typically before any call to `update()` which triggers migration.
- **Order is not important** - attributes can be registered in any order (from the manual at line 138).
